SALSA-JAX is a derived work. It is a JAX port of HAM-SALSA, the Sectional
Aerosol module for Large Scale Applications, as distributed in the
HAM-SALSA box-model code at https://github.com/reflective-org/SALSA
(commit d87dc07). HAM-SALSA was developed by Kokkola et al. at the Finnish
Meteorological Institute (FMI) and collaborators, and is released by the
HAMMOZ Consortium under the BSD 3-Clause License. Original SALSA authors
named in the source headers include Korhonen, Kokkola, Bergman, Niskanen,
Laakso and Kuehn.

The vendored Fortran source files in this repository are taken from that
code and retain their original per-file author, copyright and
SPDX-License-Identifier headers. Those headers remain in force and must be
preserved in any redistribution.
